Reviewed October 24, 2026 against the candidate's MySQL/SQLite schemas, database code and native revision writer. This is a publication source; no external wiki update is implied.

The '''layer_sets''' table retains the older shared revisions for files, PDF pages and slides. After migration completion, those shared writes are read-only. The implemented page-owned model stores the complete snapshot in the owner's native <code>layers</code> slot alongside its main content. A legacy row ID/revision counter is '''not''' a native owner page ID or MediaWiki revision ID.

Use the native updater and [https://github.com/slickdexic/Layers/blob/codex/l01-publication-admission/docs/UPGRADING.md migration/recovery procedure], not SQL copied from this reference. Updater/schema installation is separate from completion. Back up the complete wiki database, uploads including old versions, configuration and matching code; this table alone or an XML export is not a complete rollback.

Types below describe the MySQL installation schema; SQLite has its own aligned installation file. The retained successful MySQL upgrade does not qualify every database combination.

