== Creator metadata and historical safety ==
<code>ls_user_id</code> identifies the author of a particular revision. The legacy JSON <code>ownerId</code> is server-generated original-creator user metadata, not the native owning page ID. It survives pruning; clients cannot assign it. Older rows may lack it. Only a retained revision 1 establishes legacy creator ownership; a later editor must not inherit ownership merely because older rows were deleted.

Before completion, legacy names/rows can be renamed, pruned or deleted. After completion, native file deletion preserves retained shared rows; source access and cache invalidation are separate checks. Never use legacy row IDs as durable native-history references or purge retained rows as an upgrade step.

Native set identity includes the owning page and file/slide/name scope. Every page of one PDF set shares the same visible name; <code>ls_page</code> in this legacy table is an internal source page number, not a different visible set name or native page ID. The same visible name on another file or owner is independent.

See [https://github.com/slickdexic/Layers/blob/codex/l01-publication-admission/docs/PAGE_OWNED_API_GUIDE.md the native API guide] for complete-snapshot publication and [https://github.com/slickdexic/Layers/blob/codex/l01-publication-admission/docs/MILESTONE_1_RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md the release checklist] for acceptance. Schema documentation does not authorize direct database edits.
